    },
    "html": "\n  <div class=\"hero-meta\">\n    <span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"2\">Level 2 - Beginner</span>\n    <span class=\"time\">45 min</span>\n    <span class=\"chip\">Concurrency for LLD</span>\n    <span class=\"chip\">Asked by Uber, Microsoft, Walmart</span>\n  </div>\n  <h1>Thread Safety Basics: Races, Visibility &amp; Atomicity</h1>\n  <p class=\"lead\">Why two threads can sell the same last seat, why <code>count++</code> loses updates, and why a thread can spin forever on a flag that another thread already set. You will leave with the three words every concurrency follow-up is built on (atomicity, visibility, ordering), the Java memory model's happens-before rules, and exactly what <code>volatile</code> does and does not buy you.</p>\n"
